SUMMARY:Beyond Academia Job Search Series: Navigating the Non-Academic Jo
 b Market
DESCRIPTION:Navigating the non-academic job market can be a complex\, evo
 lving process. Graduate career advisers will share: - Factors to conside
 r and strategies for finding career opportunities outside academia. - Ho
 w the Campus Recruiting Program works\, recruitment timelines for differ
 ent industries\, how to engage with employers and what to keep in mind w
 hen considering offers. - How to make the most of employer information s
 essions\, coffee chats\, career fairs and other recruiting events for in
 ternship and job opportunities. This event is part of the Beyond Academi
 a Job Search series. All sessions are 12-1 p.m. - CVs & Resumes - Wednes
 day\, Sept. 9 - Navigating the Non-Academic Job Market - Thursday\, Sept
 . 22 - How to “Do” Networking - Tuesday\, Oct. - Humanities and Soci
 al Science Research Careers Outside Academia - Tuesday\, Oct. 20 - STEM 
 Research Careers Outside Academia - Thursday\, Oct. 22 This p\nRegister:
  https://princeton.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1978227\nhttps://careerd
 evelopment.princeton.edu/events/beyond-academia-job-search-series-naviga
 ting-non-academic-job-market
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/beyond-academia-job-se
 arch-series-navigating-non-academic-job-market
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
