  careers have centered around the arts. Panelists will discuss their car
 eer paths and answer questions. A reception will follow the panel. Moder
 ated by Veronica White ’98\, curator of teaching and learning at the P
 rinceton University Art Museum and lecturer in the Department of Art & A
 rchaeology. Panelists: - Anna Berghuis '19\, visual artist - Zoe Kwok \\
 *13\, Nancy and Peter Lee Senior Curator of Asian Art\, Princeton Univer
 sity Art Museum - Penelope Tang '04\, interior designer - Caressa Yan '1
 5\, associate director\, Gladstone Gallery Presented as part of the Arts
  At Work program by the Center for Career Development\, Lewis Center for
  the Arts\, and Student Advisory Board (SAB) of the Princeton University
  Art Museum. This program is part of the G. S. Beckwith Gilbert ‘63 Le
 cture Series. This program is open to all Princeton Universit\nAudience:
  Graduate Students\, Undergraduate Students\nRegister: https://princeton
 .joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1988939\nhttps://careerdevelopment.princet
 on.edu/events/arts-work-princeton-alumni-arts-panel
