SUMMARY:Career Essentials: Writing a Cover Letter
LOCATION:Frist Campus Center\, Class of 1952 Room
DESCRIPTION:Cover letters can be intimidating when you’re unsure what t
 o say beyond what is already on your resume. A strong cover letter helps
  an employer understand not only what you’ve done\, but also what make
 s you a strong candidate. This introductory session also offers an oppor
 tunity to brainstorm ideas of what to include in a cover letter. In this
  program\, you will learn: 1. The purpose of a cover letter and when emp
 loyers use it 2. The structure and format an effective cover letter 3. H
 ow to customize a cover letter to each unique opportunity 4. How to deve
 lop accomplishment stories that strengthen your application This program
  is open to all Princeton University undergraduates regardless of identi
 ty. Email [careerdevelopment@princeton.edu](mailto:careerdevelopment@pri
 nceton.edu) to request accommodations at least two weeks prior to the pr
 ogram.\nRegister: https://app.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1977163\nhttp
 s://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/career-essentials-writing-cov
 er-letter
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/career-essentials-writ
 ing-cover-letter
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
