SUMMARY:Arts at Work: Feeding the Arts with Jared Harbour '22
LOCATION:Lewis Arts Complex W331
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an informal career conversation over dinner with 
 Jared Harbour ‘22\, a writer\, producer and choreographer from New Yor
 k. Jared is a JD/MFA candidate at Columbia University. In 2022\, he co-f
 ounded Earthbound Studio\, a dance-based production company that endeavo
 rs to shed light on the current relationship between dancers and executi
 ves\, aiming to empower artists to reclaim creative and legal ownership 
 over their work. Dinner will be provided. Advanced registration is requi
 red. Arts at Work brings together Princeton alumni\, students\, and othe
 r creative professionals through speaker and panel discussions\, artists
 ’ showcases\, social events\, workshops and seminars. It is sponsored 
 by the Lewis Center for the Arts and the Center for Career Development. 
 This program is open to all Princeton University undergraduate and gradu
 ate students regardless of identity. Email [careerdevelopment\nAudience:
