SUMMARY:Crafting Your Applications for Public Service & Nonprofit Careers
LOCATION:Center for Career Development\, Conference Room
DESCRIPTION:Have you participated in service or community-based activitie
 s and wondered how they could connect to future opportunities? Or comple
 ted an SSII\, LENS\, nonprofit\, public service or other mission-driven 
 internship? Join us to reflect on what you learned\, connect it to your 
 values and future goals and craft a compelling story for employers. This
  interactive workshop will help you look back on your experience\, look 
 ahead to future opportunities and create a narrative you can use in netw
 orking\, interviews and application materials. We'll also prepare you fo
 r the upcoming Public Service Career Day (https://princeton.joinhandshak
 e.com/edu/events/1977054) by helping you communicate your experiences ef
 fectively with alumni and employers. By the end of the workshop\, you'll
  have: - A stronger personal narrative that connects your service experi
 ence to your future pursuits. - An elevator pitch/talk\nRegister: https:
 //app.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1992682\nhttps://careerdevelopment.pr
 inceton.edu/events/crafting-your-applications-public-service-nonprofit-c
 areers
